{
  "title": "Things to Be Kept in Mind for Good Memory",
  "data": "In an earlier section of al-Baqiyat al-Salihat, the author refers to a prayer to be offered for gaining a good memory: see [Namaz for Gaining Intelligence and Good Memory](F46), and also [Dua & Medicine for Good Memory](E81).\nFinally, it is advised to avoid the things that cause forgetfulness and dullness, such as:\n(1) eating sour apples, green coriander, cheese, and food left over by mice,\n(2) urinating into still water,\n(3) reading the inscriptions on graves,\n(4) walking between two women (for men),\n(5) throwing live lice on the ground,\n(6) neglecting to trim one's nails,\n(7) giving up the midday nap,\n(8) committing acts of disobedience frequently,\n(9) occupying oneself with worries and complaints about worldly affairs,\n(10) being excessively busy,\n(11) looking at crucified persons, and\n(12) walking among a train of camels."
}
